# What does not belong in the container build context.
#
# **.git stays.** Go reads the repository to stamp the commit into the binary,
# and without it `/qsp --version` reports the release with no commit — which is
# half of what §7's deploy check needs, and was the state of every container
# image built before 0278.
#
# Everything here is either a local secret, a local artefact, or something the
# build cannot use. Keeping them out is not only about size: `.env` holds an
# operator's own settings and has no business being copied into a build, even
# one whose final stage is `scratch` and keeps nothing from it.

# Local environment and configuration. The .example files are tracked and are
# the ones a reader should see.
deploy/docker/.env
qsp.json
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Build output from a workstation. The image builds its own.
/qsp
/qsp-*
/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Editors.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
